<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu al-Fath Dawud</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu al-Fath Dawud was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/multan">Multan</a> in the early 11th century, of the dynasty that had held the city since the late 10th century. Allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a>, he was attacked by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> in 1006, and Mahmud annexed Multan around 1010, persecuting its Ismailis and making the region a province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghaznavid-empire">Ghaznavid Empire</a>.</p></div>
